  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>daaf6c1000c7874cec56e6756c441045</srcmd5>
    <version>0.5.2</version>
    <time>1785601996</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.5.2

Source moves from the PyPI sdist to the upstream traceloop/openllmetry
monorepo archive (tag v0.62.1, subdirectory
packages/opentelemetry-semantic-conventions-ai).

Rationale, also recorded as a prominent comment in the spec: upstream bumped
this package's in-tree version to 0.5.2 on 2026-06-15 (commit d7aaf6cc) but
never published 0.5.2 to PyPI, whose newest sdist is still 0.5.1. A
%{version}-derived files.pythonhosted.org URL therefore 404s. The monorepo
tag is held in its own %{monorepo_ver} macro so it, not %{version}, is what
moves on the next update. Gentoo's GURU overlay packages 0.5.2 the same way.

Dependency floors raised to match upstream: opentelemetry-sdk &gt;= 1.42.0 and
opentelemetry-semantic-conventions &gt;= 0.63b1 (Factory has 1.43.0 and 0.64b0).
requires-python is now &gt;=3.10; the singlespec builds only python313 and
python314, so no flavour falls below that floor.

Local aarch64 build against openSUSE_Tumbleweed: %check runs the upstream
suite, 249 tests pass on both flavours; rpmlint 0 errors, 0 warnings, 0
badness. Built RPM verified as version 0.5.2 with the correct dist-info.</comment>
    <requestid>1368785</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="3" vrev="2">
    <srcmd5>fc7882d4175a48165f39d74012b724c5</srcmd5>
    <version>0.5.2</version>
    <time>1790585237</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update openllmetry monorepo 0.62.1 -&gt; 0.62.3 in devel:languages:python.

This is a macro-only update and Version: deliberately stays at 0.5.2. The
in-tree packages/opentelemetry-semantic-conventions-ai/pyproject.toml declares
0.5.2 at BOTH v0.62.1 and v0.62.3, and hatchling derives the dist-info
directory name from that in-tree version, so %files'
opentelemetry_semantic_conventions_ai-%{version}.dist-info glob only matches
while the two agree. The single spec change is
%define monorepo_ver 0.62.1 -&gt; 0.62.3. Flagging the unchanged Version: so it
is not mistaken for an empty change.

The shipped subdirectory is byte-identical between the two tags (diff -r over
packages/opentelemetry-semantic-conventions-ai, clean), so this refresh
carries no code change. The two upstream fixes in 0.62.2 and 0.62.3 — &quot;stop
entity names leaking onto sibling and parent spans&quot; (#4405) and &quot;register
instrumentation in commitizen version files&quot; (#4408) — are in traceloop-sdk
and the openai-agents / litellm instrumentation packages, which this package
neither builds nor ships, so they are not credited here.

Requires floors were re-derived from the 0.62.3 tarball's own metadata rather
than inherited: opentelemetry-sdk &gt;= 1.42.0 and
opentelemetry-semantic-conventions &gt;= 0.63b1. The upstream `&lt;2` ceiling on
the sdk is deliberately not encoded — it is a preemptive cap, not a floor,
and encoding it would open an unresolvable window on the next sdk major.

Built green natively on aarch64 against openSUSE:Factory:ARM standard aarch64:
rpmlint 0 errors / 0 warnings / 0 badness, %check 249 passed on each of
python313 and python314. Against the currently shipped Factory RPM the new
build is artifact-neutral: identical file list, identical Requires, rpmlint
line identical including the filtered count.

No tracker surfaces this package, so this bump has to be found by reading the
spec. No CVE or GHSA in the crossed range. No bugzilla bug references the
package, so none is cited.
</comment>
    <requestid>1380940</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="4" vrev="3">
